course: dictionary
lesson: 10214
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Titania is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. A word like that is called a proper noun. Context helps you work out what kind of name it is. In «Uranus's moons are named after characters from Shakespeare and Alexander Pope, such as Miranda, Titania and Oberon», the clues are «moons», «Uranus» and «named after characters», so Titania is a moon.
explain: Titania can also be a character in a story. In Shakespeare's play «A Midsummer Night's Dream», Titania is the queen of the fairies and the wife of Oberon. In the play, a magic flower makes her fall in love with Bottom, a man with a donkey's head. The words around the name tell you which Titania is meant.
explain: When you read a name you do not know, ask: is it a person, a place, or a thing? The capital letter is your first clue. Then look at the words around it. Titania is a name, but the context tells you whether it is a fairy queen or a moon.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Titania» is a proper noun.
fact: «Titania» means the queen of the fairies in Shakespeare's play «A Midsummer Night's Dream».
fact: «Titania» is also the largest moon of the planet Uranus.
fact: Uranus's moons are named after characters from Shakespeare and Alexander Pope, such as Miranda, Titania and Oberon.
exercise: «Uranus's moons are named after characters from Shakespeare and Alexander Pope, such as Miranda, Titania and Oberon.» What kind of thing is Titania in this sentence? | A famous actor in Shakespeare's theatre | A kind of flower | A town in Scotland | *A moon of the planet Uranus
exercise: In «A Midsummer Night's Dream», who is Titania? | A donkey | A cloud that brings rain | A boy who goes to school | *The queen of the fairies
exercise: Why does Titania start with a capital letter? | *It is a name, a proper noun | It shows that Titania is a verb | It is a very important word | It is the first word of every sentence
test: Titania is the wife of which fairy king? | Bottom | Miranda | Puck | *Oberon
test: Which planet is Titania a moon of? | Mars | Saturn | *Uranus | Neptune
exam: Ella's friend is called Titania, so what does the capital T tell you? | It shows a colour | It shows a question | It shows an action word | *It shows a name
